[{:db/id "q-121517/selection/66736252f18499cc2804196f97bcc5d148f56e758bfca4b340e05188d7b7bd18" :answer/id #uuid "d32a5dd5-a34f-5f2d-831e-7317b1b6e73b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{3/4}(-{x}^{2}+2x-6)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121517/selection/9b2c5bca9a3bd65a75767f8ed6fd80aaaeca99d50bd1add3c844b23aeea2dfa6" :answer/id #uuid "7ba6270e-1c65-5526-8e14-b85b0b7c39aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{3/4}^{1}(-8{x}^{2}-3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121517/selection/a9e78eb1cdf90a86a8187ba160bdfe049177f6aea162ecea84a2ac696e15b72c" :answer/id #uuid "3dcb7b46-232a-586c-af00-748069ef18ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-4{x}^{2}-x+4)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121517/selection/e5a2851211f542fd9cfcf106c2f7275665ee6e84243495971caacd862330bd9f" :answer/id #uuid "fcdf8ae2-e353-5d35-97e1-4d825481885c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}-2x+6)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121517/selection/68a8df4fdb540ecbc528a243a3e5c984bc43b9f3844c18c4a60e85d673faf5cc" :answer/id #uuid "e7a7e746-e6b3-50bb-b723-4f710817d632" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1/4}^{3/4}(8{x}^{2}+x-3)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121517/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "290f832c-5316-5e4e-8a45-7de3f3173b83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121517/selection/e5a2851211f542fd9cfcf106c2f7275665ee6e84243495971caacd862330bd9f" :answer-field/choices ["q-121517/selection/66736252f18499cc2804196f97bcc5d148f56e758bfca4b340e05188d7b7bd18" "q-121517/selection/9b2c5bca9a3bd65a75767f8ed6fd80aaaeca99d50bd1add3c844b23aeea2dfa6" "q-121517/selection/a9e78eb1cdf90a86a8187ba160bdfe049177f6aea162ecea84a2ac696e15b72c" "q-121517/selection/e5a2851211f542fd9cfcf106c2f7275665ee6e84243495971caacd862330bd9f" "q-121517/selection/68a8df4fdb540ecbc528a243a3e5c984bc43b9f3844c18c4a60e85d673faf5cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121517" :question/id #uuid "1495ffd4-708e-5569-a19d-b4ce8001edba" :question/math-academy-id "q-121517" :question/problem "Which integral gives the area of the finite region bounded between $y=8{x}^{2}-4$ and $y=2-2x?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/b2f34492ce184169d0e720d5a2214a356236b56d6e20bd8ece584b967f074e64.png)\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-2x & =8{x}^{2}-4 \\\\ 8{x}^{2}+2x-6 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{{2}^{2}-4\\cdot 8\\cdot (-6)}}{2\\cdot 8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 14}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-1$ to $x=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, let's draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/94243d27b465eca7957731385b2fe13fae36b811079d3077e2e093aa19d81ad3.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=8{x}^{2}-4,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=2-2x.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}[\\,(2-2x)-(8{x}^{2}-4)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}-2x+6)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121517/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e016cedd-0206-555c-8934-c6d19566d547"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121517"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121566/selection/b84d3a44d8b8c21be6f14a897e0a62b0b41df629ee647a5432551e8ad2e694b6" :answer/id #uuid "fa07377b-3bd3-5e51-bab3-af0a96068486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{4/5}(4{x}^{2}-x+5)\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121566/selection/dd01d67007cce3b8e454637b05a724b6acd21a5c3fc92250cb21bcfa3c77f6bd" :answer/id #uuid "73516eb3-9dc5-5773-819c-7d52696e0ae5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-5/4}^{1}(4{x}^{2}+x-5)\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121566/selection/0483ed1fbad303bda6477560ba729ea49d55e1b336063137fb960247531ff01e" :answer/id #uuid "42551b9f-abde-5f3c-8eb6-5688a1c996a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{5/4}(-4{x}^{2}-x+5)\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121566/selection/7b57a6e60db1a3e6eab2db28a062b2b425e4a2e1614dac809517dd7867dc2667" :answer/id #uuid "c63ecd13-53f8-5eb9-b484-f05af70dae96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}(-4{x}^{2}+x+5)\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121566/selection/b84f6708855576fb037aaa5bb0ed6b501775c2703f6efed81c405d735f251b99" :answer/id #uuid "75594be6-5839-5706-9bdf-2a9cf4607bf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}(4{x}^{2}-x-5)\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121566/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f4d607-ef7b-5645-a072-8c0f866eed83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121566/selection/7b57a6e60db1a3e6eab2db28a062b2b425e4a2e1614dac809517dd7867dc2667" :answer-field/choices ["q-121566/selection/b84d3a44d8b8c21be6f14a897e0a62b0b41df629ee647a5432551e8ad2e694b6" "q-121566/selection/dd01d67007cce3b8e454637b05a724b6acd21a5c3fc92250cb21bcfa3c77f6bd" "q-121566/selection/0483ed1fbad303bda6477560ba729ea49d55e1b336063137fb960247531ff01e" "q-121566/selection/7b57a6e60db1a3e6eab2db28a062b2b425e4a2e1614dac809517dd7867dc2667" "q-121566/selection/b84f6708855576fb037aaa5bb0ed6b501775c2703f6efed81c405d735f251b99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121566" :question/id #uuid "a08163fa-4d1f-55bf-a571-4e4e9630646e" :question/math-academy-id "q-121566" :question/problem "Which integral gives the area of the finite region bounded by $y=2{x}^{2}-3x$ and $y=5-2{x}^{2}-2x?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/9a4de823003f0461231c355a43ba9845358ec4a3767ca59c2ba2206456620373.png)\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-3x & =5-2{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x-5 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}-4\\cdot 4\\cdot (-5)}}{2\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-1$ to $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, let's draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/94b0113f7ca9ffeca11398cce06995fa4a7e5cb3f39b3021d5d6ec56746b75ee.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=2{x}^{2}-3x,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=5-2{x}^{2}-2x.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}[\\,(5-2{x}^{2}-2x)-(2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}(-4{x}^{2}+x+5)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121566/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e016cedd-0206-555c-8934-c6d19566d547"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121585/selection/198e23089eaac2c24aa0521b5e4270d877579d1783a35cc741dd46af60d91e60" :answer/id #uuid "6df5d658-8a88-569f-a6b5-e8ca18e71cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121585/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "610f1d4a-aa4e-576b-85e8-e09d78fda35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121585/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "761624e2-5716-5636-b33d-fb9a4df2696c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121585/selection/d07c3286538006b3c100c9c4401e8b04ade74e340cd39e154db0ad27535b7124" :answer/id #uuid "2d309c77-9608-5ba3-8956-9c2d3f5cb945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{62}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121585/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "5213550d-4fb9-5591-980a-92aa2ae603f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e745bd6-4ba1-5bfc-a396-75968cb361a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121585/selection/198e23089eaac2c24aa0521b5e4270d877579d1783a35cc741dd46af60d91e60" :answer-field/choices ["q-121585/selection/198e23089eaac2c24aa0521b5e4270d877579d1783a35cc741dd46af60d91e60" "q-121585/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-121585/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" "q-121585/selection/d07c3286538006b3c100c9c4401e8b04ade74e340cd39e154db0ad27535b7124" "q-121585/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121585" :question/id #uuid "c84d87bd-9d44-56d4-92d0-f67ba8ac76ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-121585" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the finite region bounded by the curves $y=2{x}^{2}-2$ and $y=6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/0fd8a89bdcad9f1b20c9fd35df9aa209a5e551d5d7a7c97f62103e23e7ae9741.png)\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-2 & =6 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-2$ to $x=2.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, we draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/83e8d6af5284006b4caad6b1a96cb1298f7c7672d6c35fa652359d3a0b28e037.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=2{x}^{2}-2,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=6.$\n\nTherefore, we can find the area, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[\\,(6)-(2{x}^{2}-2)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(8-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3})|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =[8\\cdot 2-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {2}^{3}]-[8\\cdot (-2)-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =(16-\\frac{16}{3})-(-16+\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fa1bebf-4af0-5a5c-962c-8a88f8392776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121772/selection/db5b999b06edd2d25dce0527c14ecdefdd736de5a07467801d68fac699433e7d" :answer/id #uuid "9e1ea365-e568-5919-b405-f3c90be18740" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{251}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121772/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "dcfa1c93-7144-5efd-a7f6-dd4226d855db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121772/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer/id #uuid "9bb367bd-abc7-594b-ae48-30d1fd779359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121772/selection/d8180fb40af5867fc6ed0537e9ad01a16006bf53f8c78b6e3cc5f547b07ffefb" :answer/id #uuid "a076330d-e49e-53cf-a0b7-93b2b2c02acb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{256}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121772/selection/198e23089eaac2c24aa0521b5e4270d877579d1783a35cc741dd46af60d91e60" :answer/id #uuid "f0b13a58-949d-59bd-b81d-b7146f916083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121772/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03e42d4f-1366-595e-be2b-243c9be99de4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121772/selection/d8180fb40af5867fc6ed0537e9ad01a16006bf53f8c78b6e3cc5f547b07ffefb" :answer-field/choices ["q-121772/selection/db5b999b06edd2d25dce0527c14ecdefdd736de5a07467801d68fac699433e7d" "q-121772/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" "q-121772/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" "q-121772/selection/d8180fb40af5867fc6ed0537e9ad01a16006bf53f8c78b6e3cc5f547b07ffefb" "q-121772/selection/198e23089eaac2c24aa0521b5e4270d877579d1783a35cc741dd46af60d91e60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121772" :question/id #uuid "c2412cf4-7cbd-5fc0-a3ce-3581348a7006" :question/math-academy-id "q-121772" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the finite region bounded by the curves $y={x}^{2}-10$ and $y=6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/9248483d8b55c2ac61fcc3c1f11fee0eabee92794eaacd1fb2e37fff68cec289.png)\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10 & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-4$ to $x=4.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, we draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/173d726e4b0ecee37d8b7ca8878f5bc5934a069dc48a2b9d18e28d72f3b04f7e.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y={x}^{2}-10,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=6.$\n\nTherefore, we can find the area, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}[\\,(6)-({x}^{2}-10)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}(16-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(16x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})|}_{-4}^{4} \\\\  & =[16\\cdot 4-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3}]-[16\\cdot (-4)-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-4)^{3}] \\\\  & =(64-\\frac{64}{3})-(-64+\\frac{64}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{256}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121772/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fa1bebf-4af0-5a5c-962c-8a88f8392776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121772"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-356029/field-1/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "29ee47f7-9e46-528f-bf70-34a3947a8bb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-356029/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2245c1f-04cb-53e9-b142-66a2689d6ad3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-356029/field-1/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer-field/choices ["q-356029/field-1/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-356029" :question/id #uuid "dabd07a4-7ceb-5d01-9a56-3f969a97f96a" :question/math-academy-id "q-356029" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the finite region bounded by the curves $y={x}^{2}-3$ and $y=1.$\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/664fcc791ec42b4ec40ed3fc7033fa601d646c9900632864122d31fd01a2cf61.png)\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-3 & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-2$ to $x=2.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, we draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/1d10b1994774239767578417bc5f0b74a6a7369005a73fbac859574c9d5d36e0.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y={x}^{2}-3,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=1.$\n\nTherefore, we can find the area, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[\\,(1)-({x}^{2}-3)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(4x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =[4\\cdot 2-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{3}]-[4\\cdot (-2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =(8-\\frac{8}{3})-(-8+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-(-\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-356029/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fa1bebf-4af0-5a5c-962c-8a88f8392776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-356029"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
